course: dictionary
lesson: 7153
title: Perfection: no faults at all
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perfection is a noun. It means the state of being perfect, with no faults at all. You can also use it for someone or something that is an ideal example: «The cake was perfection.» Here the cake is so good that it could not be any better.
explain: Perfection can also mean the act of making something perfect. In «the perfection of a skill», the word means the slow work of getting better and better at something, like practising a piano piece until every note is smooth.
explain: Be careful: wanting perfection can make people stressed. «Bodies like change more than perfection: slouching for a while does no harm, but sitting in any one position for hours does, so get up, stretch and move often.» The author is saying that movement is healthier than trying to hold one perfect position.
explain: In cooking and sport, «cooked to perfection» and «played to perfection» mean done very well. In church, Christians believe God is perfect, and some speak of God's perfection. Look at the words around perfection to tell which meaning is being used.
fact: Perfection means the state of being perfect, with no faults at all.
fact: Perfection can mean something that is an ideal example, like «The cake was perfection.»
fact: Perfection can also mean the act of making something perfect, like «the perfection of a skill».
fact: «Cooked to perfection» and «played to perfection» mean done very well.
fact: Chasing perfection can make people stressed; it is fine to make mistakes and learn from them.
exercise: «The cake was perfection.» What does perfection mean in this sentence? | Something that is nice but not special | A small, plain cake | A cake with a few mistakes in it | *Something perfect, an ideal example
exercise: «Bodies like change more than perfection: slouching for a while does no harm, but sitting in any one position for hours does.» Why does the author say to move often? | Perfect posture is always the best | Moving makes you perfect | Slouching is harmful for a few minutes | *Sitting in one position for hours does harm
exercise: Mia says, «The pie was cooked to perfection.» What does she mean? | It was made by a famous chef only | *It was made very well, with no faults | It was burnt on purpose | It was eaten all at once
test: Chasing perfection can make people stressed. What is a healthier idea? | Never try anything unless you are sure you will get it perfect | Stress is the same as perfection | Mistakes mean you have failed completely | *It is fine to make mistakes and learn from them
test: Which word means the same as perfection, a state with no faults at all? | *Flawlessness | Nervousness | Laziness | Carelessness
exam: Some people speak of God's perfection. In this sense, what does perfection mean? | Being very late | Being a pretty picture | *Being without fault, complete and perfect | Being in a hurry
